_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"180f65f75d004d18\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3832126306538889, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17960596950555557, \"vector_similarity\": 0.85829484, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (27)\\n\\n**linux-foundation-easycla[bot]** — 2025-10-14T04:01:31Z\\n\\n<a href=\\\"https://easycla.lfx.linuxfoundation.org/#/?version=2\\\"><img src=\\\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cla-project-logo-prod/cla-signed.svg?v=2\\\" alt=\\\"CLA Signed\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" width=\\\"328\\\" ></a><br/><br />The committers listed above are authorized under a signed CLA.<ul><li>:white_check_mark: login: nicksherron / name: Nick Sherron  (43d6c1b5f0c27c73a83543d0f681e2dc766d86dc, 6c560fe0a618c400f5961126b3daf71074a98113, ebe29b975966edee33e7c0e2fdcca7c89710fd63)</li></ul>\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T04:35:20Z\\n\\nThe current changes do not guarantee thread safety.\\n\\nAdditionally, I lean towards the view that for infrastructure-level components or frameworks, there is no need to consider the concurrency safety of `req.WithContext` and `req.Context()`.\\n\\nOnce these components introduce certain mechanisms for concurrency safety, it may lead to performance degradation.\\n\\nFor users pursuing high performance, such performance degradation is unacceptable. Moreover, once implemented, users have no choice but to use these mechanisms.\\n\\nTherefore, I prefer to leave the decision of whether to ensure concurrency safety to the users themselves, and let them implement these mechanisms on their own.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston discuss 27 linux foundat easycla bot 2025 10 14t04 01 31z a href http easycla lfx linuxfound org version 2 img src http s3 amazonaw com cla project logo prod cla sign svg v2 alt cla sign align left height 28 width 328 a br br the committ list abov are author under a sign cla ul li white _ check _ mark login nicksherron name nick sherron 43d6c1b5f0c27c73a83543d0f681e2dc766d86dc 6c560fe0a618c400f5961126b3daf71074a98113 ebe29b975966edee33e7c0e2fdcca7c89710fd63 li ul flc1125 2025 10 14t04 35 20z the current chang do not guarante thread safeti addit i lean toward the view that for infrastructur level compon or framework there is no need to consid the concurr safeti of req withcontext and req context onc these compon introduc certain mechan for concurr safeti it may lead to perform degrad for user pursu high perform such perform degrad is unaccept moreov onc implement user have no choic but to use these mechan therefor i prefer to leav the decis of whether to ensur concurr safeti to the user themselv and let them implement these mechan on their own\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"9d57dc1fb2041765\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3794865436538889, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17960596950555557, \"vector_similarity\": 0.84587455, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Defer Provides No Benefit\\n\\nLet's analyze what the current code does:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() {\\n\\n      c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx)  // ← Restores AFTER request completes\\n\\n  }()\\n\\n  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(savedCtx, propagation.HeaderCarrier(c.Request.Header))\\n\\n  // ...\\n\\n  c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // ← Sets new context\\n\\n  c.Next()  // ← Processes request\\n\\n  // When we return, defer runs and \\\"restores\\\" the old context\\n\\n```\\n\\n  Question: Why restore the context after the request is complete?\\n\\n  - After c.Next() returns, the request has been fully processed\\n\\n  - Gin doesn't reuse *gin.Context instances across requests\\n\\n  - Downstream handlers may spawn goroutines that read c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  - The deferred write to c.Request races with those goroutine reads\\n\\n  - There is no code that benefits from this restoration\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Performance Argument is Backwards\\n\\nThe current code with the defer is slower than the fix:\\n\\n  Current code overhead:\\n\\n  - Allocates closure for defer\\n\\n  - Saves context reference\\n\\n  - Executes deferred function on return\\n\\n  - Calls WithContext() twice (once to set, once to \\\"restore\\\")\\n\\n  Fixed code:\\n\\n  - No defer\\n\\n  - No closure allocation\\n\\n  - One fewer WithContext() call\\n\\n  - No unnecessary context copy\\n\\n Benchmark comparison (removing defer should show improvement):\\n\\n  -  Current: ~3 allocations per request\\n\\n  -  Fixed:   ~2 allocations per request\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"label mileston the defer provid no benefit let s analyz what the current code doe go savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx restor after request complet ctx cfg propag extract savedctx propag headercarri c request header c request c request withcontext ctx set new context c next process request when we return defer run and restor the old context question whi restor the context after the request is complet after c next return the request ha been fulli process gin doesn t reus gin context instanc across request downstream handler may spawn goroutin that read c request context the defer write to c request race with those goroutin read there is no code that benefit from this restor sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the perform argument is backward the current code with the defer is slower than the fix current code overhead alloc closur for defer save context refer execut defer function on return call withcontext twice onc to set onc to restor fix code no defer no closur alloc one fewer withcontext call no unnecessari context copi benchmark comparison remov defer should show improv current 3 alloc per request fix 2 alloc per request\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"0e4329537c0aa36a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3645360192526281, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16551307036089727, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8289229, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> Could you turn your gist into a test that can run on CI, and add it to this PR?\\n\\nSure, I'd be happy to.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T07:42:26Z\\n\\n> ```go\\n\\n> }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n>           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n>           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> ```\\n\\nI believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\nI'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing data race\\\". Rather, it removes unnecessary code that has unintended side effects.\\n\\ne.g., The defer restoration discards any context modifications made within the `otelgin` middleware chain (including downstream handlers).\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T07:47:23Z\\n\\n> > ```go\\n\\n> > }(c.Request.Context(), c.Writer.Status(), time.Since(start))\\n\\n> >           //  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n\\n> >           //  THIS RACES WITH otelgin's defer!\\n\\n> > ```\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I believe my understanding aligns with yours. I approve this PR and agree with the changes.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I'd like to clarify that the primary value isn't about \\\"fixing data race\\\". Rather, it removes unnecessary code that has unintended side effects.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> e.g., The defer restoration discards any context modifications made within the `otelgin` middleware chain (including downstream handlers).\\n\\nSounds good, thank you for your time on this. I also added the test @dmathieu requested. If you want me to make any changes to it just let me know.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**codecov[bot]** — 2025-10-14T07:50:11Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"could you turn your gist into a test that can run on ci and add it to this pr sure i d be happi to flc1125 2025 10 14t07 42 26z go c request context c writer status time sinc start this race with otelgin s defer i believ my understand align with your i approv this pr and agre with the chang i d like to clarifi that the primari valu isn t about fix data race rather it remov unnecessari code that ha unintend side effect e g the defer restor discard ani context modif made within the otelgin middlewar chain includ downstream handler nicksherron 2025 10 14t07 47 23z go c request context c writer status time sinc start this race with otelgin s defer i believ my understand align with your i approv this pr and agre with the chang i d like to clarifi that the primari valu isn t about fix data race rather it remov unnecessari code that ha unintend side effect e g the defer restor discard ani context modif made within the otelgin middlewar chain includ downstream handler sound good thank you for your time on this i also ad the test dmathieu request if you want me to make ani chang to it just let me know codecov bot 2025 10 14t07 50 11z sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"998f12a39803f3d9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34287636945010647, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13732727207158074, \"vector_similarity\": 0.82249093, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```go\\n\\nfunc Middleware() {\\n\\n    savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n    defer func() {\\n\\n        c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx)  // ← Step 5: WRITE\\n\\n    }()\\n\\n    c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // Step 1\\n\\n    c.Next()                                 // Step 2: All handlers/middleware run\\n\\n    // Step 3: Handler spawned goroutine that reads c.Request.Context()\\n\\n    // Step 4: Handler returns\\n\\n    // Step 5: defer runs and WRITES to c.Request\\n\\n    // Step 6: Background goroutine READS c.Request ← **RACE**!\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\nThe defer IS the concurrent modification. It writes to c.Request after handlers complete, while\\n\\nbackground goroutines spawned by those handlers may still be reading it.\\n\\nThe fix removes this write:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nfunc Middleware() {\\n\\n    reqCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n    ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(reqCtx, ...)\\n\\n    c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // Step 1: Set once\\n\\n    c.Next()                                 // Step 2: Handlers run\\n\\n    // Step 3: Handler spawns goroutine\\n\\n    // Step 4: Handler returns\\n\\n    // Step 5: No defer, no write ← NO RACE\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\nProof: TestMiddleware_MinimalRaceRepro demonstrates exactly this:\\n\\n- Handler spawns goroutine that accesses c.Request.Context()\\n\\n- Handler returns\\n\\n- Old code: defer writes → DATA RACE\\n\\n- Fixed code: no write → PASS\\n\\nFurthermore this isn't my \\\"specific case\\\" - this is how Go middleware is supposed to work. The defer breaks standard Go patterns that every Go developer uses.\\n\\nGo's own documentation recommends this pattern\\n\\nFrom https://pkg.go.dev/context:\\n\\n>   \\\"Incoming requests to a server should create a Context, and outgoing calls to servers should accept a Context. The chain of function calls between them must propagate the Context,\\n\\n>   optionally replacing it with a derived Context...\\\"\\n\\n> \\n\\nPassing c.Request.Context() to goroutines is the recommended approach for:\\n\\n  - Timeouts\\n\\n  - Cancellation\\n\\n  - Tracing (which is what otelgin does!)\\n\\nOther popular Gin middleware use this exact pattern!\\n\\nExample using an extremely common pattern in production:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n func main() {\\n\\n      router := gin.New()\\n\\n      // Setup OpenTelemetry tracing (standard pattern)\\n\\n      router.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-service\\\"))\\n\\n      // Add async logging middleware (also standard pattern)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"go func middlewar savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx step 5 write c request c request withcontext ctx step 1 c next step 2 all handler middlewar run step 3 handler spawn goroutin that read c request context step 4 handler return step 5 defer run and write to c request step 6 background goroutin read c request race the defer is the concurr modif it write to c request after handler complet while background goroutin spawn by those handler may still be read it the fix remov this write go func middlewar reqctx c request context ctx cfg propag extract reqctx c request c request withcontext ctx step 1 set onc c next step 2 handler run step 3 handler spawn goroutin step 4 handler return step 5 no defer no write no race proof testmiddlewar _ minimalracerepro demonstr exact this handler spawn goroutin that access c request context handler return old code defer write data race fix code no write pas furthermor this isn t my specif case this is how go middlewar is suppos to work the defer break standard go pattern that everi go develop us go s own document recommend this pattern from http pkg go dev context incom request to a server should creat a context and outgo call to server should accept a context the chain of function call between them must propag the context option replac it with a deriv context pass c request context to goroutin is the recommend approach for timeout cancel trace which is what otelgin doe other popular gin middlewar use this exact pattern exampl use an extrem common pattern in product go func main router gin new setup opentelemetri trace standard pattern router use otelgin middlewar my servic add async log middlewar also standard pattern\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"f31afd660670eb11\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32875320418259935, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1279320059751419, \"vector_similarity\": 0.797336, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"nam