efit of it, I'm going to assume it was added for hygiene to avoid leaking the modifications out of the intended request's middleware chain.\\n\\n@flc1125 what are your thoughts, even if it doesn't provide thread safety it does seem valid\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T05:01:16Z\\n\\n> I'm going to assume it was added for hygiene to avoid leaking the modifications out of the intended request's middleware chain.\\n\\nI agree with this situation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T05:06:09Z\\n\\nI'm confused about this \\\"doesn't provide thread safety\\\" claim. I'm starring at a test failure due to data race when running `go test -race`  in one of my projects that clearly points the finger to the code I removed as being the culprit. When I do a `go mod -replace` using my change in this PR the race goes away. \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T05:09:52Z\\n\\n> I'm confused about this \\\"doesn't provide thread safety\\\" claim. I'm starring at a test failure due to data race when running `go test -race` in one of my projects that clearly points the finger to the code I removed as being the culprit. When I do a `go mod -replace` using my change in this PR the race goes away.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"ctx cfg propag extract savedctx after use context direct correct reqctx c request context ctx cfg propag extract reqctx the behavior is ident except no race condit better perform simpler code test pas with race conclus this is a straightforward bug fix that 1 remov unnecessari code that caus a race 2 improv perform fewer alloc no defer overhead 3 fix a2 year old issu 4588 4 follow preced from previous race fix in this project 5 enabl ci to enforc race free code there is no downsid to this chang and signific benefit i respect request approv to merg akats7 2025 10 14t04 58 07z hi nicksherron it s a fair question i also don t realli see the benefit of it i m go to assum it wa ad for hygien to avoid leak the modif out of the intend request s middlewar chai