{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"dmathieu October 17 2025 close #8014 comment reason closing"},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"dmathieu October 17 2025 close #8014 comment reason closing"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThere seems to be absolutely no reason to save and restore the request context in a deferred function. The way it was done before could (and did) lead to a race condition because when c.Next() is called, the request context could be changed by another goroutine, and then the deferred function would modify the request while another goroutine is using it. \\n\\nI can't for the life of me figure out what benefit the previous code was trying to achieve, other than maybe trying to minimize the context size in memory, but that seems unnecessary and not worth the risk of a data race. Furthermore, I'm not even sure that said memory savings would pay off because when running `go build -gcflags=\\\"-m\\\"` against the current implementation you can see that context and request escapes to heap:\\n\\n```\\n\\n./gin.go:84:37: \\\"nil context\\\" escapes to heap\\n\\n./gin.go:84:37: new(http.Request) escapes to heap\\n\\n```\\n\\nThis is likely negligible but I figured I'd add it for more context, no pun intended 😉\\n\\nPerhaps the goal was not that of performance/memory savings but instead to \\\"restore\\\" the context. If so, this is also incorrect because in Gin, there's no need to restore the context - each request gets its own *gin.Context .\\n\\nFinally, this change actually more closely matches the [code cited](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-go/blob/8fb554ff7cf694267f9077ae35e27ce4689ed8b6/contrib/gin-gonic/gin/gintrace.go) as the \\\"inspiration\\\" for the otelgin package. \\n\\nWithout this change, we unfortunately cannot run our tests with the race detector enabled and is not production ready due to not being goroutine safe.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston descript there seem to be absolut no reason to save and restor the request context in a defer function the way it wa done befor could and did lead to a race condit becaus when c next is call the request context could be chang by anoth goroutin and then the defer function would modifi the request while anoth goroutin is use it i can t for the life of me figur out what benefit the previous code wa tri to achiev other than mayb tri to minim the context size in memori but that seem unnecessari and not worth the risk of a data race furthermor i m not even sure that said memori save would pay off becaus when run go build gcflag m against the current implement you can see that context and request escap to heap gin go 84 37 nil context escap to heap gin go 84 37 new http request escap to heap this is like neglig but i figur i d add it for more context no pun intend perhap the goal wa not that of perform memori save but instead to restor the context if so this is also incorrect becaus in gin there s no need to restor the context each request get it own gin context final this chang actual more close match the code cite http github com datadog dd trace go blob 8fb554ff7cf694267f9077ae35e27ce4689ed8b6 contrib gin gonic gin gintrac go a the inspir for the otelgin packag without this chang we unfortun can not run our test with the race detector enabl and is not product readi due to not be goroutin safe\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"a69b1eaa6d5ba704\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2688805352796265, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1099743218280379, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6396617, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:43:31Z\\n\\nJust found an open 2 year old issue this would fix #4588 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:56:41Z\\n\\nThanks for the quick response @flc1125 , but I would like to offer a rebuttal. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## This PR Fixes an Existing Bug, Not Introducing New Safety Mechanisms\\n\\nI respectfully disagree with the characterization that this PR \\\"introduces mechanisms for concurrency safety.\\\" The opposite is true: this PR removes problematic code that causes a data race.\\n\\nThe current code has a real, reproducible race condition reported in issue #4588 (open for 2 years). The race detector fails consistently. This is not theoretical—it violates Go's memory model.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 43 31z just found an open 2 year old issu this would fix 4588 nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 56 41z thank for the quick respons flc1125 but i would like to offer a rebutt sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston this pr fix an exist bug not introduc new safeti mechan i respect disagre with the character that this pr introduc mechan for concurr safeti the opposit is true this pr remov problemat code that caus a data race the current code ha a real reproduc race condit report in issu 4588 open for 2 year the race detector fail consist this is not theoret it violat go s memori model sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"79dd2c776e5b2e7f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26555004491526424, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08843878987894893, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67880964, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-03]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-10-10\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3390010099  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-10T13:10:44Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-10T14:04:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-09\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n## Agenda Items\\n\\n### 1. Milestone Progress Review\\n\\n**Current milestone status:**\\n\\n- 17 items still open in the milestone\\n\\n- Most PRs are in review phase or awaiting final approvals\\n\\n**Key items discussed:**\\n\\n#### Expose temporality selector functions\\n\\n- **Status:** Under discussion, may not be accepted in current form\\n\\n- **Discussion:** Tyler and David discussed whether to expose temporality selector parsing functions for configuration\\n\\n- **Decision:** Not recommended for inclusion in SDK. Users should use full OpenTelemetry configuration file format instead of custom configuration snippets\\n\\n- **Rationale:** Want to standardize on OTel configuration format rather than supporting fragmented approaches\\n\\n- **Action:** Tyler to respond with feedback about standardization preference\\n\\n#### Prometheus Exporter Migration\\n\\n- **Status:** Implementation complete, needs deprecation decision\\n\\n- **Discussion:** Need to decide on deprecating existing configuration options\\n\\n- **Decision:** Tyler supports deprecation before marking as stable\\n\\n- **Next steps:** Handle in next milestone\\n\\n#### Error Handling for Prometheus\\n\\n- **Status:** PR ready for review, waiting for conversation resolution\\n\\n- **Action:** David to review and potentially merge\\n\\n#### High mutex contention in metric sums\\n\\n- **Status:** Resolved via PR #7427\\n\\n- **Action:** Close issue\\n\\n### 2. Optimization Work Discussion\\n\\n**David's current work:**\\n\\n- Implementing lockless exponential histogram\\n\\n- Fun and challenging optimization project\\n\\n- Building on previous optimization PRs\\n\\n**PR Reviews needed:**\\n\\n- **PR #7474:** Exemplar reservoir optimization (approved by Tyler, needs second approval)\\n\\n- **PR #7443:** Histogram optimization (needs review, has race condition issue identified)\\n\\n**Technical discussion on PR #7443:**\\n\\n- Tyler identified potential race condition in min/max tracking with `isSet` flag\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 03 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 1010 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3390010099 author pellar creat 2025 10 10t13 10 44z updat 2025 10 10t14 04 27z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 09 attende tyler yahn david ashpol bryan boreham agenda item 1 mileston progress review current mileston status 17 item still open in the mileston most pr are in review phase or await final approv key item discuss expos tempor selector function status under discuss may not be accept in current form discuss tyler and david discuss whether to expos tempor selector pars function for configur decis not recommend for inclus in sdk user should use full opentelemetri configur file format instead of custom configur snippet rational want to standard on otel configur format rather than support fragment approach action tyler to respond with feedback about standard prefer prometheus export migrat status implement complet need deprec decis discuss need to decid on deprec exist configur option decis tyler support deprec befor mark a stabl next step handl in next mileston error handl for prometheus status pr readi for review wait for convers resolut action david to review and potenti merg high mutex content in metric sum status resolv via pr 7427 action close issu 2 optim work discuss david s current work implement lockless exponenti histogram fun and c